  "notes": [
    "Every valid text decodes and re-encodes byte for byte; its Drive file name is fmsx-<type>-<id>.json (section 8.1).",
    "Members are written in one fixed order: the wrapper as schemaVersion, type, writtenAt, ttlSeconds, record; each record body as listed in its vector.",
    "Timestamps are written UTC with milliseconds and Z, and read with or without milliseconds.",
    "A broadcast descriptor is carried verbatim as a JSON object, never as a string.",
    "Every tolerated text decodes and re-encodes to its canonical text: unknown members are dropped, an unknown presence reads offline, a plays pair with a blank member and an out-of-range publicPort are dropped, a resource without access decodes with no descriptor (section 15 item X: listed, cannot be attached).",
    "Every skipped text decodes to nothing and is never an error."
  ],
